{#- The dashboard, rendered by tools/report.py from out/development/evaluation.json.

    Plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript with eleven values dropped in, each named at
    the one place it is rendered: favicon_href, noscript_rows, evaluation_json,
    shadow_json, redteam_json, holdout_json, chain_json, model_json, logo_svg,
    hero_scope, airgap_svg. Autoescaping is off — each is HTML or JSON built on purpose — and
    a name the renderer does not pass raises.

    Jinja reads three pairs of characters here: double braces, brace-percent and
    brace-hash. The JavaScript below contains none of them outside the eleven
    values; write `{ {` or a template literal before introducing one.
-#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Vasool &mdash; agent report card</title>
    <meta name="description" content="A payment-recovery agent measured against a protocol registered before it ran: what it recovered, what it refused, what still beats it, and a ledger you can verify in your browser.">
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{ favicon_href }}">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:title" content="Vasool — agent report card">
    <meta property="og:description" content="A payment-recovery agent measured against a protocol registered before it ran: what it recovered, what it refused, what still beats it, and a ledger you can verify in your browser.">
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://sriramvarun0636.github.io/Vasool/">
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://sriramvarun0636.github.io/Vasool/assets/dashboard.png">
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="The Vasool report card: Rs 40.97 Cr recovered in the development cohort with 0 safety violations in 1,000 seeds. Beneath it, falsification criterion F6 has fired — 5 of 8 recovery comparisons fail to survive a ±50% move of the outcome model — so the recovery figures are presented as what this simulator produced, not findings. The fresh holdout's Rs 66.68 Cr describes an earlier agent and is not added. Beside the headline, the record read off the artifacts: the section 2a safety predicate held on 1,000 of 1,000 seeds, pass^100 of 1.00, 23 of 24 attacks survived the registered criterion with 1 open and named, 1 registered criterion fired of the 7 evaluated, 10 of the 11 outcome-model parameters tagged as guesses, re-run ledgers identical byte for byte, and a chain of 15 guards of which 11 cite a statute.">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;450;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Serif+Devanagari:wght@500&text=%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%82%E0%A4%B2&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
           The report card: volume one of two. docs/theatre/ is volume two and
           is built from the same tokens, so a reader moving between them stays
           in one document. Shared tokens are marked; do not let them drift.

           The page reads as an instrument. It spent a year as a printed
           dossier instead -- Newsreader at display size, cream rules,
           print-scale whitespace -- and that set the register wrong: a serif
           masthead over a payments ledger reads as a thesis defence rather
           than as something running in production.

           The type is one superfamily doing two jobs. IBM Plex Sans writes;
           IBM Plex Mono measures. Every figure a reader is invited to check
           is set in the mono at whatever size it needs -- the headline total,
           the yield rates, the tiles, the record -- because a number you can
           trace should look like a number that came out of a file, and it
           puts the hero on the same grid as the tables beneath it. The two
           are siblings by design, which is the whole reason to spend a page
           on one family rather than pair two.

           There is no ambient light here and no gradient anywhere: a soft
           glow behind a dark hero is the decoration every product page
           reaches for, and this one has figures to spend the attention on
           instead. A panel is spent on two things only: a drawing that needs
           a field of its own, and a control a reader operates. Figures that
           are merely read are ruled, because a page where every block is a
           card has no hierarchy left to spend. Blue is the agent's own colour, from
           its mark, marking Vasool's figures and nothing else; green, amber
           and red remain verdicts.
           ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
        :root {
            /* shared with docs/theatre/index.html */
            --ink: #06090F;
            --ink-lift: #0A0E17;
            --panel: #0D1220;
            --panel-lift: #141B2D;
            --hairline: rgba(255,255,255,0.065);
            --hairline-firm: rgba(255,255,255,0.13);
            --signal-blue: #3D6FF7;
            --blue-lift: #7098FF;
            --compliant-green: #35C98A;
            --violation-red: #F0555A;
            --caution-amber: #FFB224;
            --paper: #F2F4F8;
            --body-text: #C8D1E1;
            --dim: #8C99B0;
            --dimmer: #5D6B85;
            --na: #4C5875;
            --font-display: 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
            --font-body: 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
            --font-mono: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
            --font-deva: 'Noto Serif Devanagari', 'Kohinoor Devanagari', 'Devanagari MT', serif;
            /* Every figure a reader is invited to check is set in the mono, at
               whatever size it needs. That is the one typographic rule here:
               words in the sans, measurements in the face that came out of the
               file. */
            --font-figure: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;

            /* local */
            --vasool: #8FB2FF;          /* the brand blue, lifted to read as type on ink */
            --vasool-wash: rgba(61,111,247,0.085);
            --radius: 8px;
            --radius-sm: 6px;
            --measure: 70ch;

            /* A panel is a flat surface one step off the ground and a hairline
               around it. No gradient, no drop shadow, no highlight along the
               top edge: those are three ways of faking a light source, and a
               page whose claim is that nothing here is decorative should not
               open by faking one. Depth comes from the step in value alone. */
            --panel-border: 1px solid var(--hairline);

            /* Data-visualisation tokens. The diverging pair blue<->red is
               unchanged by the 2026-09-22 restyle, on purpose: its registered
               separation -- CVD dE 19.2, normal-vision dE 29.0 -- is a
               property of the two colours and not of what sits behind them,
               so it survives a change of ground untouched. What did change is
               the ground, from #121B30 to #0D1220, and darker only helps:
               contrast rose from 4.71 to 5.13 for the blue and 5.31 to 5.78
               for the red, both still well over the 3:1 floor. Status colours
               always ship with an icon and a word, never hue alone. */
            --viz-ahead: #3987e5;
            --viz-behind: #e66767;
            --viz-zero: #3A3F48;
            --viz-grid: rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
            --viz-axis: rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
            --viz-muted: #7C879B;
            --status-good: #35C98A;
            --status-warning: #FFB224;
            --status-critical: #F0555A;

            /* the partition's five buckets, in the order the table reads */
            --part-recovered: #35C98A;
            --part-blocked: #3D6FF7;
            --part-escalated: #A78BFA;
            --part-exhausted: #e66767;
            --part-awaiting: #26314C;
        }

        * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
        html { background: var(--ink); scroll-behavior: smooth; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
        body {
            background-color: var(--ink);
            color: var(--body-text);
            font-family: var(--font-body);
            font-size: 15.5px;
            line-height: 1.6;
            letter-spacing: -0.006em;
            -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
            text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
            display: flex;
            min-height: 100vh;
            /* The spine is fixed, so the column it sits beside is inset here
               rather than by a margin on the column itself — which would pin
               the page to the left edge and leave a wide screen half empty. */
            padding-left: 72px;
        }
        :focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--blue-lift); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 4px; }
        code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.88em; color: #B9C4DA; }
        strong, b { font-weight: 600; }
        h1, h2, h3 { text-wrap: balance; }

        /* ---------- the spine: one mark per exhibit, the current one lit ---- */
        #spine {
            width: 72px;
            gap: 6px;
            border-right: 1px solid var(--hairline);
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            padding: 104px 0 40px;
            position: fixed;
            height: 100vh;
            z-index: 60;
            background: transparent;
            /* `left` is not optional here. Without it a fixed element keeps its
               static position, which for the body's first flex child is x=72 --
               the far side of the 72px `body` already reserves -- so the rail
               sat on top of the column and painted over the first character of
               every line. `.topbar` has assumed `left:72px` since it was
               written, which is the same geometry said twice. */
            left: 0;
        }
        /* The letter, in the mono, at index size. A rail of set capitals in a
           display serif is the loudest thing a printed dossier does; a rail of
           bare dots is the quietest thing a landing page does, and carries no
           information at all. The letter is what the exhibit is called, so the
           rail says it -- small, dim, and in the face the rest of the page
           uses for anything it wants read literally. */
        .spine-mark {
            position: relative;
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 500;
            letter-spacing: 0.06em;
            color: var(--dimmer);
            text-decoration: none;
            width: 26px; height: 22px;
            display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
            border-radius: 3px;
            transition: color .18s ease, background-color .18s ease;
        }
        .spine-mark:hover { color: var(--paper); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); }
        .spine-mark.is-here { color: var(--signal-blue); }
        /* A tick on the rule beside the current letter: the rail is a scale
           and this is the reading on it. */
        .spine-mark.is-here::before {
            content: ''; position: absolute; left: -9px; top: 50%;
            width: 5px; height: 1px; background: var(--signal-blue);
            transform: translateY(-50%);
        }
        /* Hovering a letter names the exhibit it jumps to. */
        .spine-mark::after {
            content: attr(data-label);
            position: absolute; left: 34px; top: 50%;
            transform: translate(-4px, -50%);
            white-space: nowrap;
            font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500;
            letter-spacing: -0.005em;
            color: var(--paper); background: var(--panel-lift);
            border: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
            padding: 5px 10px;
            opacity: 0; pointer-events: none;
            transition: opacity .16s ease, transform .16s ease;
        }
        .spine-mark:hover::after, .spine-mark:focus-visible::after { opacity: 1; transform: translate(0, -50%); }
        .spine-progress {
            margin-top: auto;
            width: 1px;
            height: 84px;
            background: var(--hairline-firm);
            overflow: hidden;
        }
        .spine-progress-fill {
            width: 100%; height: 0%;
            background: var(--signal-blue);
            transition: height .12s linear;
        }

        /* ---------- the column --------------------------------------------- */
        #content {
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 88px 56px 48px;
            flex-grow: 1;
            max-width: 1320px;
            /* Without this a flex item's min-width resolves to `auto`, so the
               container refuses to shrink below its widest child and the whole
               page scrolls sideways instead of the one wide box inside it. */
            min-width: 0;
        }

        /* ---------- the masthead ---------------------------------------------- */
        /* Fixed rather than sticky, and full-bleed from the spine to the
           window's edge: a rule that stops at the text column reads as a stray
           line rather than as the edge of a masthead. Its contents sit in the
           same measure as the page below it. */
        .topbar {
            position: fixed; top: 0; left: 72px; right: 0; z-index: 50;
            background: rgba(6, 9, 15, 0.72);
            backdrop-filter: blur(16px);
            -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px);
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
        }
        .topbar .bar {
            display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 22px; flex-wrap: wrap;
            max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 13px 56px;
        }
        /* The mark is the word's own first letter — the Devanagari va — so it
           is set at the wordmark's cap height and on its baseline rather than
           floated beside it. The glyph fills 44 of the viewBox's 64 units and
           sits 8 units clear of the bottom, which is what the size and the
           nudge are computed from: 26px box → 17.9px of ink against a 17.5px
           cap, dropped 3px so the bowl lands on the baseline. */
        .lockup {
            display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px;
            text-decoration: none; color: var(--paper);
        }
        .lockup .vasool-mark {
            display: block; width: 22px; height: 22px; flex: none;
            transform: translateY(2px);
        }
        .wordmark {
            font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: -0.028em; line-height: 1;
            color: var(--paper);
        }
        .volumes { display: inline-flex; gap: 20px; margin-left: 10px; }
        .volumes a {
            position: relative;
            font-size: 13.5px; text-decoration: none; color: var(--dim);
            padding: 4px 0;
            transition: color .16s;
        }
        .volumes a:hover { color: var(--paper); }
        .volumes a[aria-current="page"] { color: var(--paper); }
        .volumes a[aria-current="page"]::after {
            content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: -15px; height: 2px;
            background: var(--signal-blue);
        }
        .topbar .spacer { flex: 1 1 auto; }
        .toplink {
            font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--dim); text-decoration: none;
            transition: color .16s;
        }
        .toplink:hover { color: var(--paper); }

        /* ---------- provenance mode ------------------------------------------
           Every figure on this page carries the path it came from; the toggle
           reveals them all at once. This is the whole thesis of the project
           applied to its own report card: a number you cannot trace is not a
           result.
           -------------------------------------------------------------------- */
        .prov-toggle {
            display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px;
            padding: 7px 12px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); cursor: pointer;
            background: none;
            border: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm); color: var(--paper);
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: 0.02em;
            transition: border-color 0.18s ease, background 0.18s ease;
        }
        .prov-toggle:hover { border-color: var(--dim); }
        .prov-toggle[aria-pressed="true"] {
            border-color: var(--signal-blue);
            background: rgba(61,111,247,0.18);
        }
        .prov-dot {
            width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
            background: var(--viz-muted); flex: none;
        }
        .prov-toggle[aria-pressed="true"] .prov-dot { background: var(--signal-blue); }
        [data-src] { position: relative; }
        body.provenance [data-src] {
            outline: 1px dashed rgba(61,111,247,0.55);
            outline-offset: 3px;
            border-radius: 2px;
        }
        .prov-path {
            display: none;
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10.5px; line-height: 1.45;
            font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.01em; text-transform: none;
            font-variation-settings: normal;
            color: var(--signal-blue); word-break: break-all;
            margin-top: 6px; opacity: 0.95;
        }
        body.provenance .prov-path { display: block; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
        /* In running prose a block path would break the sentence in half, so
           there it sits inline behind the figure it belongs to. */
        body.provenance .dek .prov-path,
        body.provenance .hero-sub .prov-path,
        body.provenance .hero-note .prov-path,
        body.provenance .viz-caption .prov-path,
        body.provenance .footnote .prov-path { display: inline-block; margin: 0 0 0 7px; }
        .prov-banner {
            display: none;
            border: 1px solid rgba(61,111,247,0.4); background: rgba(61,111,247,0.08);
            border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 18px 22px; margin-bottom: 40px;
            font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.7;
            color: var(--paper);
        }
        body.provenance .prov-banner { display: block; }

        #fallback-warning {
            display: none;
            background-color: rgba(244, 196, 48, 0.1);
            color: var(--caution-amber);
            border: 1px solid var(--caution-amber);
            padding: 12px 24px;
            margin-bottom: 32px;
            border-radius: var(--radius);
            font-family: var(--font-mono);
            font-size: 13px;
        }

        /* ---------- hero: the result, then the record ---------------------------- */
        .hero {
            scroll-margin-top: 88px;
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.18fr) minmax(330px, 0.82fr);
            gap: clamp(32px, 4vw, 64px);
            align-items: stretch;
            margin-bottom: 88px;
        }
        .hero-main { min-width: 0; }
        /* A slug line, the way a filing is headed: which report, which cohort,
           which agent, separated by rules. It was briefly a rounded badge --
           the eyebrow pill every landing page opens with -- which is both
           louder than this and says less. */
        .kicker {
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.05em;
            color: var(--dim); margin-bottom: 22px;
            padding-bottom: 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
        }
        .kicker .sep { color: var(--na); margin: 0 10px; }
        /* The headline figure in the mono, tracked hard. Plex Mono's fixed
           advance is what makes this read as a measurement rather than a
           slogan -- the rupee sign, the digits and the unit all sit on the
           same grid the tables below use. */
        #hero-money {
            font-family: var(--font-figure);
            font-size: clamp(46px, 7.2vw, 84px);
            font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: -0.055em;
            line-height: 1.0;
            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums;
            color: var(--paper);
        }
        .hero-sub { margin-top: 18px; font-size: 16.5px; color: var(--dim); }
        .hero-sub #hero-violations { color: var(--compliant-green); }
        .dek {
            margin-top: 26px; max-width: 56ch;
            font-size: 18.5px; line-height: 1.5; letter-spacing: -0.014em;
            color: #B4C0D4;
        }
        .dek b { color: var(--paper); font-weight: 600; }
        .dek .behind { color: var(--viz-behind); }
        .hero-acts { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 34px; align-items: center; }
        .cta {
            display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.012em; text-decoration: none;
            border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 11px 17px;
            border: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
            background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); color: var(--paper);
            transition: background-color .16s, border-color .16s;
        }
        .cta:hover { border-color: var(--dim); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06); }
        .cta.primary { background: var(--signal-blue); border-color: var(--signal-blue); color: #fff; }
        .cta.primary:hover { background: var(--blue-lift); border-color: var(--blue-lift); }
        .cta .glyph { font-size: 10px; line-height: 1; }
        .hero-note {
            margin-top: 12px; max-width: 72ch;
            font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--dimmer);
        }
        #hero-split { margin-top: 34px; }
        .hero-note b { color: var(--dim); font-weight: 500; }

        /* The record, set as a statement: a heavy rule, then one ruled line
           per verdict, figure to the right. Each figure is read from an
           artifact. */
        /* The record is read, not operated, so it is ruled rather than boxed:
           a firm rule, then one line per verdict with the figure right-aligned
           in the mono. It was briefly a card, which made the hero read as a
           landing page with a stat panel beside the pitch. */
        .glance { align-self: start; }
        /* The rule sits under this label, not over it, so that it lands at the
           same height as the rule under the slug line in the column beside it
           and the two read as one line drawn across the page. Both are set in
           the mono at a line and a half, so matching the padding matches the
           y; if either type size moves, the other padding moves with it. */
        .glance .gh {
            padding: 0 0 15px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            color: var(--dimmer);
        }
        .glance .grow:first-of-type { border-top: 0; }
        .grow {
            display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, auto); gap: 2px 18px;
            align-items: baseline;
            padding: 13px 0 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
        }
        .grow .gl { font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--paper); letter-spacing: -0.012em; }
        .grow .gv {
            grid-row: span 2; align-self: center; text-align: right;
            font-family: var(--font-figure); font-size: 21px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1;
            letter-spacing: -0.04em; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums;
            color: var(--paper); white-space: nowrap;
        }
        /* The path under a figure is longer than the figure; without a cap it
           would set this column's width and squeeze the label beside it. */
        .grow .gv { max-width: 230px; }
        .grow .gv .prov-path { text-align: right; }
        .grow .gs { font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--dimmer); }
        .grow .gs .ok { color: var(--compliant-green); }
        .grow .gs .warn { color: var(--status-warning); }
        .grow .gs .bad { color: var(--viz-behind); }
        .glance .gfoot {
            padding: 14px 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
            font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--dimmer);
        }
        .glance .gfoot b { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--dim); font-weight: 400; word-break: break-all; }

        /* ---------- exhibits ------------------------------------------------- */
        .exhibit {
            margin-bottom: 96px;
            position: relative;
            scroll-margin-top: 88px;
        }
        .ex-head { margin-bottom: 26px; max-width: 900px; }
        /* §2a claims hold whatever the simulator does; §2b figures depend on
           it. EVALUATION.md requires the two not to look alike, so the mark is
           solid for one and hollow for the other, in a verdict colour. */
        .band-tag {
            display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
            color: var(--dim); margin-bottom: 16px;
            padding: 5px 10px 5px 8px; border-radius: 3px;
            border: 1px solid var(--hairline); background: none;
        }
        .band-tag::before {
            content: ''; width: 7px; height: 7px; flex: none; border-radius: 2px;
            border: 1.5px solid var(--dimmer);
        }
        .band-independent .band-tag { color: var(--compliant-green); border-color: rgba(53,201,138,0.32); }
        .band-independent .band-tag::before { background: var(--compliant-green); border-color: var(--compliant-green); }
        .band-dependent .band-tag { color: var(--status-warning); border-color: rgba(255,178,36,0.32); }
        .band-dependent .band-tag::before { border-color: var(--status-warning); }
        /* The caption as an exhibit is captioned in a filing: the label in
           small capitals, the title in the display face, on one line. */
        .exhibit-title {
            display: block;
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 500;
            letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--dimmer);
            line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 8px;
        }
        .ex-name {
            font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(27px, 3vw, 37px);
            font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.032em; line-height: 1.1;
            color: var(--paper);
            margin-left: 0;
        }
        .viz-caption, .standfirst {
            font-size: 15.5px;
            line-height: 1.7;
            color: var(--dim);
            margin-bottom: 32px;
            max-width: var(--measure);
        }
        .viz-caption strong, .standfirst strong { color: var(--paper); font-weight: 500; }
        .viz-caption em { color: #B9C4DA; }
        .sub-h {
            margin: 64px 0 10px;
            font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: -0.024em; color: var(--paper);
        }
        .sub-lede { margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--dim); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.68; max-width: var(--measure); }
        .sub-lede strong { color: var(--paper); font-weight: 500; }
        .footnote {
            margin-top: 18px; max-width: 84ch;
            font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--dimmer);
        }
        .footnote strong, .footnote b { color: var(--dim); font-weight: 500; }

        /* ---------- Exhibit A: three arms, one universe, one statement -------- */
        .versus {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: minmax(180px, 1.15fr) repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
            border: var(--panel-border);
            border-radius: var(--radius);
            overflow: hidden;
            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums;
        }
        .versus > div {
            padding: 13px 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
            min-width: 0;
        }
        .versus .vl { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--dim); align-self: stretch; display: flex; align-items: center; }
        .versus .vh { padding-top: 16px; padding-bottom: 16px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.028); }
        /* The header row's first cell is empty -- the corner above the measure
           names -- and it carries the band too. Without this the tint started
           at the second column and the header read as a seam rather than as a
           row. */
        .versus .vl.head { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.028); }
        .versus .vh .role { font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--paper); }
        .versus .vh .arm { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--dimmer); margin-top: 2px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
        .versus .vc { text-align: right; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--paper); }
        .versus .is-vasool { background: var(--vasool-wash); }
        .versus .vh.is-vasool .role { color: var(--vasool); }
        .versus .rate { padding-top: 20px; padding-bottom: 18px; }
        .yield-number {
            font-family: var(--font-figure);
            font-size: clamp(27px, 3.1vw, 39px);
            font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: -0.05em;
            line-height: 1;
            color: var(--paper);
        }
        .yield-number.yield-blue { color: var(--vasool); }
        .arm-bar { margin-top: 12px; height: 4px; border-radius: 999px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.07); overflow: hidden; }
        .arm-bar i { display: block; height: 100%; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--dim); }
        .is-vasool .arm-bar i { background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--signal-blue), var(--blue-lift)); }
        .verdict { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; }
        .verdict.ok { color: var(--compliant-green); }
        .verdict.bad { color: var(--viz-behind); }
        .vc.hot { color: var(--viz-behind); }
        .vc.zero { color: var(--compliant-green); }

        /* ---------- visualisations --------------------------------------------- */
        .viz-figure { margin-top: 8px; }
        .viz-legend {
            display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 22px;
            font-size: 13px;
            color: var(--dim); margin: 4px 0 18px;
        }
        .viz-legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
        .viz-swatch { width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 2px; flex: none; }
        .viz-scroll, .world-scroll {
            max-width: 100%;
            overflow-x: auto;
            -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
        }
        .plot-card {
            border: var(--panel-border); border-radius: var(--radius);
            background: var(--panel);
            padding: 20px 20px 10px;
        }

        /* forest plot */
        .forest { width: 100%; min-width: 640px; font-family: var(--font-mono); display: block; }
        .forest .f-label { fill: var(--paper); font-size: 13px; }
        .forest .f-sub { fill: var(--viz-muted); font-size: 11px; }
        .forest .f-value { font-size: 12.5px; }
        .forest .f-tick { fill: var(--viz-muted); font-size: 11px; }
        .forest .f-grid { stroke: var(--viz-grid); stroke-width: 1; }
        .forest .f-zero { stroke: var(--viz-axis); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-dasharray: 3 3; }
        .forest .f-ci { stroke-width: 2; stroke-linecap: round; }
        .forest .f-row-hit { fill: transparent; cursor: default; }
        .forest .f-row-hit:hover + .f-row-bg { fill: rgba(255,255,255,0.035); }
        .forest .f-row-bg { fill: transparent; pointer-events: none; }
        details.tv-toggle { margin-top: 14px; }
        details.tv-toggle > summary {
            cursor: pointer; font-size: 13px; color: var(--dim); padding: 6px 0;
        }
        details.tv-toggle > summary:hover { color: var(--paper); }

        /* sweep survival grid */
        .grid-wrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto; gap: 6px 14px; align-items: center; }
        .grid-arm {
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--paper);
            white-space: nowrap; text-align: right;
        }
        .grid-cells { display: flex; gap: 2px; min-width: 0; }
        .grid-cell {
            flex: 1 1 0; height: 22px; min-width: 3px; border-radius: 1px;
            background: rgba(255,255,255,0.09);
        }
        .grid-cell.flip { background: var(--viz-behind); }
        .grid-count {
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--dim);
            white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
        }
        .grid-count.flip { color: var(--viz-behind); }

        /* An exhibit whose artifact is absent says so in the space the figure
           would have filled. Prose describing a figure that is not on the page
           is the failure this replaced. */
        .empty-state {
            border: 1px dashed var(--hairline-firm); border-radius: var(--radius);
            background: none;
            padding: 28px 30px; max-width: 900px;
        }
        .empty-state .es-t {
            font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 19px; font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: -0.024em; color: var(--paper);
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }
        .empty-state .es-b { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--dim); max-width: var(--measure); }
        .empty-state .es-b code { font-size: 0.86em; color: var(--status-warning); }

        /* falsification board: seven registered criteria, one ruled line each */
        .fboard { border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm); }
        .frow {
            display: grid; grid-template-columns: 56px minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
            gap: 22px; align-items: baseline;
            padding: 18px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
        }
        .frow .fid {
            font-family: var(--font-figure); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3;
            letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        }
        .frow .fname { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--paper); }
        .frow .fthr {
            display: block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px;
            color: var(--dimmer); margin-top: 5px; line-height: 1.55;
        }
        .frow .fwarn {
            display: block; margin-top: 10px; max-width: 72ch;
            font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--status-warning);
        }
        .frow .fverdict {
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; text-align: right;
            white-space: nowrap; display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-end;
        }
        .frow.warn { background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255,178,36,0.08), rgba(255,178,36,0) 70%); }
        .frow.idle .fname, .frow.idle .fid { color: var(--dimmer) !important; }

        /* figure strips: a few measured figures in a row, divided by rules */
        .tiles {
            display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr));
            border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
        }
        .tile { padding: 20px 24px 20px 0; }
        .tile + .tile { padding-left: 24px; border-left: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
        .tile .tv {
            font-family: var(--font-figure); font-size: 27px; font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: -0.045em;
            color: var(--paper); line-height: 1.1;
            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums;
        }
        .tile .tl { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--dimmer); margin-top: 9px; line-height: 1.5; }

        /* ---------- the guard chain, drawn from the code ------------------------ */
        /* Fifteen links in the order they run: read down, then across. */
        .chain {
            list-style: none; margin-top: 26px;
            columns: 3; column-gap: 40px;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
        }
        .chain li {
            break-inside: avoid;
            display: grid; grid-template-columns: 30px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0 10px;
            padding: 12px 0 13px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
        }
        .chain .ix {
            font-family: var(--font-figure); font-size: 12px; color: var(--dimmer);
            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums; line-height: 1.55;
        }
        .chain .gn { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--paper); line-height: 1.4; }
        .chain .gn .gid { color: var(--dimmer); font-size: 11px; margin-left: 6px; }
        .chain .gs { grid-column: 2; margin-top: 3px; font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--dim); }
        .chain li.house .gn { color: #B9C4DA; }
        .chain li.house .gs { color: var(--dimmer); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; }

        /* ---------- tables ------------------------------------------------------ */
        .world-table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
            margin-top: 24px;
            font-family: var(--font-mono);
            font-size: 12.5px;
            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
        }
        .world-table th, .world-table td {
            padding: 11px 12px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
            text-align: right;
            white-space: nowrap;
        }
        /* The LLM's answer distribution is the one cell with real prose in it;
           forcing it onto one line pushes the last two columns off the page,
           and those two columns are the whole point of the table. */
        #llm-table td:nth-child(4) { white-space: normal; min-width: 190px; }
        #llm-table td:first-child, #llm-table th:first-child { white-space: normal; }
        #rt-table th:nth-child(3) { text-align: left; }
        .world-table th:first-child, .world-table td:first-child { text-align: left; padding-left: 0; }
        .world-table thead th {
            color: var(--dim);
            font-family: var(--font-body);
            font-weight: 500;
            font-size: 12.5px;
            vertical-align: bottom;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
        }
        .world-table thead th small {
            display: block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 400; font-size: 11px; color: var(--dimmer);
        }
        .world-table tbody tr:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); }
        /* Only the arm's name carries its colour. Painting a whole row green
           renders every figure in it as good news, which on these tables was
           the editorialising they exist to remove -- a count of permitted
           probes shown as a pass, censored episodes shown as wins. */
        .world-table tr.is-vasool td:first-child { color: var(--vasool); }
        .world-table tr.is-vasool td { background: var(--vasool-wash); }
        .world-table td.zero { color: var(--compliant-green); }
        .world-table td.nonzero { color: var(--viz-behind); }
        .world-table td.verdict-open { color: var(--viz-behind); }
        .world-table td.verdict-held { color: var(--compliant-green); }

        /* the partition, drawn: one bar per arm, five buckets that sum to one */
        .pbars { margin-top: 22px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 8px 16px; align-items: center; }
        .pbars .pa { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--dim); text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
        .pbars .pa.is-vasool { color: var(--vasool); }
        .pbars .pb { display: flex; height: 14px; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); }
        .pbars .pb i { display: block; height: 100%; }
        .pbars .pb i + i { box-shadow: inset 1px 0 0 rgba(6,9,15,0.9); }

        /* ---------- Exhibit F: the air gap -------------------------------------- */
        .airgap-card {
            border: var(--panel-border); border-radius: var(--radius);
            background: var(--panel);
            padding: 12px 20px 22px;
        }
        .airgap-svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 8px 0 4px; }
        .ag-h { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; fill: var(--dim); }
        .ag-c { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10.5px; fill: var(--dimmer); }
        .ag-t { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; fill: var(--body-text); }
        .ag-dim { fill: #7C8798; }
        .ag-node { fill: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); stroke: var(--hairline); }
        .ag-llm { stroke: var(--violation-red); fill: rgba(240,85,90,0.07); }
        .ag-shared { stroke: var(--caution-amber); fill: rgba(255,178,36,0.06); }
        .ag-act { stroke: var(--compliant-green); fill: rgba(53,201,138,0.05); }
        .ag-edge { stroke: var(--hairline-firm); stroke-width: 1; }
        .ag-gap { stroke: #475569; stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 3 5; }
        .ag-legend {
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.7;
            color: var(--dimmer); text-align: center; max-width: 62ch; margin: 8px auto 0;
        }
        .ag-legend code { color: var(--dim); }

        /* ---------- Exhibits H and I: the ledger, verified here ------------------- */
        .verifier-box {
            background: var(--panel);
            border: var(--panel-border);
            border-radius: var(--radius);
            padding: 26px 28px 28px;
        }
        .verifier-box .lede2 { margin-bottom: 22px; color: var(--dim); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.65; max-width: var(--measure); }
        .input-group { display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
        input[type="text"] {
            flex: 1 1 280px; min-width: 0;
            background-color: rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
            border: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
            border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
            color: #fff;
            padding: 11px 14px;
            font-family: var(--font-mono);
            font-size: 13px;
            outline: none;
        }
        input[type="text"]:focus { border-color: var(--signal-blue); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--signal-blue); }
        .btn {
            font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.012em;
            background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
            border-radius: var(--radius-sm); color: var(--paper);
            padding: 10px 16px; cursor: pointer; transition: background-color .16s, border-color .16s, color .16s;
        }
        .btn:hover:not([disabled]) { border-color: var(--dim); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06); }
        .btn.p { background: var(--signal-blue); border-color: var(--signal-blue); color: #fff; }
        .btn.p:hover:not([disabled]) { background: var(--blue-lift); border-color: var(--blue-lift); }
        .btn.danger { border-color: rgba(240,85,90,0.55); color: #FFB2B5; }
        .btn.danger:hover:not([disabled]) { border-color: var(--violation-red); color: #fff; }
        .btn[disabled] { opacity: 0.38; cursor: not-allowed; }
        #verifier-console {
            background-color: rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
            border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
            border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
            padding: 16px;
            min-height: 120px;
            font-family: var(--font-mono);
            font-size: 12.5px;
            line-height: 1.7;
            color: var(--dim);
            white-space: pre-wrap;
            overflow-wrap: anywhere;
        }
        .console-success { color: var(--compliant-green); }
        .console-error { color: var(--viz-behind); }
        /* Sixty-four hex digits, digit under digit: when one byte of the payload
           changes, you can see how little of the digest survives. */
        .hexrow { margin-top: 18px; }
        .hexrow .lb { font-size: 12px; color: var(--dimmer); margin-bottom: 6px; }
        .hexline {
            display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px clamp(6px, 0.9vw, 12px);
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: clamp(12px, 1.45vw, 18px); line-height: 1.5;
        }
        .hexline .grp { display: flex; }
        .hexline .grp span { width: 1.08ch; text-align: center; color: #B9C4DA; }
        .hexline .grp span.on { color: var(--compliant-green); }
        .hexline .grp span.off { color: #fff; background: var(--violation-red); border-radius: 1px; }

        .explorer-board {
            display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(250px, 320px) minmax(0, 1fr);
            background-color: var(--panel);
            border: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
            border-radius: var(--radius);
            overflow: hidden;
            height: 500px;
        }
        .explorer-list {
            border-right: 1px solid var(--hairline);
            overflow-y: auto;
            padding: 0 0 6px;
        }
        .explorer-summary {
            padding: 13px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
            font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--dim);
        }
        .explorer-summary b { color: var(--compliant-green); font-weight: 500; }
        .explorer-item {
            all: unset; box-sizing: border-box; display: block; width: 100%;
            position: relative; cursor: pointer;
            padding: 10px 16px 10px 38px;
            border-left: 2px solid transparent;
            font-family: var(--font-mono);
            color: var(--dim);
            transition: background-color .16s ease, color .16s ease;
        }
        /* the chain itself: each receipt hangs off the one before it */
        .explorer-item::before {
            content: ''; position: absolute; left: 18px; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 1px;
            background: var(--hairline-firm);
        }
        .explorer-item:first-of-type::before { top: 18px; }
        .explorer-item:last-child::before { bottom: calc(100% - 18px); }
        .explorer-item .dotp {
            position: absolute; left: 14px; top: 14px; width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%;
            background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
        }
        .explorer-item.ok .dotp { border-color: var(--compliant-green); background: var(--compliant-green); }
        .explorer-item.bad .dotp { border-color: var(--violation-red); background: var(--violation-red); }
        .explorer-item .r1 { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: baseline; font-size: 12px; }
        .explorer-item .r1 .oc { margin-left: auto; font-size: 11px; }
        .explorer-item .r2 { font-size: 10.5px; color: var(--dimmer); margin-top: 2px; }
        .explorer-item:hover { background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.025); color: #fff; }
        .explorer-item.active { border-left-color: var(--signal-blue); background-color: rgba(61,111,247,0.1); color: #fff; }
        .oc-executed { color: var(--compliant-green); }
        .oc-recovered { color: var(--vasool); }
        .oc-blocked { color: var(--viz-behind); }
        .oc-escalated { color: #B3A8FF; }
        .oc-other { color: var(--dim); }
        .explorer-console {
            padding: 20px 22px;
            font-family: var(--font-mono);
            font-size: 12.5px;
            line-height: 1.65;
            color: var(--body-text);
            overflow-y: auto;
            background-color: var(--ink);
            white-space: pre-wrap;
            /* The payload is compact JSON -- no spaces -- so pre-wrap finds no
               break opportunity inside a 64-char hex id and the line ran past
               the box and clipped. These are the exact bytes the hash covers;
               every one of them has to be visible. */
            overflow-wrap: anywhere;
        }
        .explorer-console .xh { display: block; color: var(--paper); margin-bottom: 4px; }
        .explorer-console .xm { display: block; color: var(--dimmer); margin-bottom: 14px; }
        .explorer-console .xb { color: #B9C4DA; }
        .explorer-console .xact { margin-top: 18px; display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; white-space: normal; }

        /* ---------- no JavaScript ----------------------------------------------- */
        .noscript-panel {
            max-width: 760px;
            margin: 48px auto;
            padding: 28px 32px;
            border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
            background: var(--panel);
            font-size: 15px;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }
        .noscript-panel h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 28px; margin: 0 0 16px; }
        .noscript-panel table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 20px 0; }
        .noscript-panel caption {
            caption-side: bottom; text-align: left; padding-top: 12px;
            font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--dim);
        }
        .noscript-panel th, .noscript-panel td {
            text-align: left; padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
        }
        .noscript-panel td { font-family: var(--font-mono); text-align: right; }

        /* ---------- colophon ------------------------------------------------------ */
        .page-footer {
            margin: 120px 0 0;
            padding: 56px 0 72px;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm);
            display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 40px 64px;
        }
        .footer-claim {
            font-family: var(--font-display);
            font-size: clamp(21px, 2.4vw, 28px);
            font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: -0.028em;
            line-height: 1.28;
            color: var(--paper);
            margin: 0 0 22px;
            max-width: 24em;
        }
        .footer-meta {
            font-size: 14px;
            line-height: 1.75;
            color: var(--dim);
            margin: 0 0 26px;
            max-width: var(--measure);
        }
        .footer-links { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--dimmer); margin: 0; line-height: 2.1; }
        .footer-links a { color: var(--dim); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-firm); }
        .footer-links a:hover { color: #fff; border-color: var(--signal-blue); }
        /* The name, glossed once, beside the mark it is drawn from. */
        .colophon-mark { text-align: right; }
        .colophon-mark .vasool-mark { width: 64px; height: 64px; display: inline-block; }
        .colophon-mark .deva {
            display: block; margin-top: 10px;
            font-family: var(--font-deva); font-size: 26px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--paper);
        }
        .colophon-mark .gloss { display: block; margin-top: 2px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--dimmer); font-style: italic; }

        /* ---------- narrow viewports ---------------------------------------------
           Wide content scrolls in its own box; the page itself never does. Anyone
           opening the Pages link on a phone once got a 1,273px page in a 390px
           window, because fixed gutters and two min-widths pushed the container
           past the viewport instead of scrolling inside it.
           ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
        .exhibit, .versus, .tiles, .grid-wrap, .chain { max-width: 100%; min-width: 0; }
        .world-table, .forest { max-width: none; }
        pre { overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; }

        @media (max-width: 1100px) {
            .chain { columns: 2; }
        }
        @media (max-width: 980px) {
            .hero { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
            .toplink { display: none; }
        }
        @media (max-width: 900px) {
            #spine { display: none; }
            body { padding-left: 0; }
            #content { padding: 74px 16px 48px; max-width: 100%; }
            .topbar { left: 0; }
            .topbar .bar { padding: 11px 16px; gap: 14px; }
            .volumes a[aria-current="page"]::after { bottom: -12px; }
            .versus { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); font-size: 12px; }
            .versus > div { padding: 11px 8px; }
            .versus .vl { font-size: 12px; }
            .yield-number { font-size: 26px; }
            .frow { grid-template-columns: 40px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 8px 14px; }
            .frow .fverdict { grid-column: 2; white-space: normal; align-items: flex-start; text-align: left; }
            .explorer-board { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); height: auto; }
            .explorer-list { max-height: 300px; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
            .explorer-console { max-height: 420px; }
            .pbars { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 3px; }
            .pbars .pa { text-align: left; margin-top: 6px; }
            .page-footer { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
            .colophon-mark { text-align: left; }
        }
        @media (max-width: 640px) {
            .chain { columns: 1; }
            .volumes { gap: 14px; margin-left: 0; }
            .prov-toggle .pt-label { display: none; }
            .tile .tv { font-size: 28px; }
            .tile { padding: 16px 12px 16px 0; }
            .tile + .tile { padding-left: 12px; }
            .grow .gv { font-size: 24px; }
            /* Four columns do not fit a phone: each measure's label takes a line
               of its own, and the three arms sit under it. */
            .versus { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
            .versus .vl { grid-column: 1 / -1; padding: 16px 0 2px; border-bottom: 0; color: var(--paper); }
            .versus .vl.head { display: none; }
            .versus .vc { text-align: left; }
        }
        @media (max-width: 420px) {
            .wordmark { font-size: 22px; }
            .lockup .vasool-mark { width: 23px; height: 23px; transform: translateY(2px); }
        }

        /* On a phone the masthead wraps to two rows -- lockup, volumes, the
           provenance toggle -- and a fixed element that grows taller than the
           padding reserved for it lands on top of the first thing on the page.
           Rather than guess a taller padding, the bar stops being fixed here
           and takes its own space in the flow, which is right for a small
           screen anyway: 90px of a 667px window is not worth spending on
           navigation that scrolls with you. */
        @media (max-width: 680px) {
            .topbar {
                position: static;
                background: none;
                backdrop-filter: none; -webkit-backdrop-filter: none;
                margin: 0 -16px 8px;
            }
            .topbar .bar { padding: 12px 16px; row-gap: 10px; }
            .volumes a[aria-current="page"]::after { bottom: -8px; }
            #content { padding-top: 0; }
        }

        @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
            *, *::before, *::after { transition: none !important; animation: none !important; }
            html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
        }

        /* Print. Readers save PDFs, and a dark ground prints as a slab of ink
           with the type knocked out of it. Scrollers are expanded because a
           clipped table in a PDF is a table nobody can check. */
        @media print {
            :root {
                --ink: #ffffff; --ink-lift: #ffffff; --panel: #ffffff; --panel-lift: #ffffff;
                --hairline: rgba(0,0,0,0.16); --hairline-firm: rgba(0,0,0,0.28);
                --paper: #111; --body-text: #111; --dim: #444; --dimmer: #666; --vasool: #1A4FC4;
            }
            body { background: #fff; color: #111; }
            #spine, .topbar, .prov-banner, .prov-path, .hero-acts, .input-group, .btn { display: none !important; }
            #content { margin: 0; padding: 0 12mm; max-width: none; }
            .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
            .exhibit { break-inside: avoid; page-break-inside: avoid; margin-bottom: 18mm; }
            .ex-head, h1, h2, h3 { break-after: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; }
            .viz-scroll, .world-scroll, .explorer-console, .explorer-list, pre {
                overflow: visible !important; max-height: none !important;
            }
            .explorer-board { height: auto !important; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
            a[href^="http"]::after { content: " (" attr(href) ")"; font-size: 10px; word-break: break-all; }
            #hero-money { color: #111; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <noscript>
        <div class="noscript-panel">
            <h1>Vasool &mdash; agent report card</h1>
